\DOC SIMPS_RULE

\TYPE {SIMPS_RULE : thm list -> thm -> thm}

\SYNOPSIS
Simplify the conclusion of a theorem with the simp set.

\DESCRIBE
{SIMPS_RULE thl th} simplifies the conclusion of {th} with the declared
simp rules and the theorems of {thl}. It is {CONV_RULE (SIMPS_CONV thl)}.

\FAILURE
Never fails, though it may leave the theorem as it was.

\EXAMPLE
{
  # SIMPS_RULE [ADD_CLAUSES] (REFL `count (Call (Cons (Num 3) Nil))`);;
  val it : thm = |- true
}

\SEEALSO
add_simp, SIMP_RULE, SIMPS_CONV, SIMPS_TAC.

\ENDDOC
